<title>PERU: Peru's October sugar output up 1.3 percent.</title>
<headline>Peru's October sugar output up 1.3 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's sugar production rose 1.3 percent in October to 628,160 tonnes, compared to the same month last year, the Agriculture Ministry said Thursday.</p>
<p>The ministry's monthly report added that sugar output for the first ten months fell to 4.931 million tonnes from 5.105 million tonnes, compared to the same period last year.</p>
<p>Total 1995 production was 6.325 million tonnes.</p>
<p>Imports of sugar rose 68.7 percent in October to $8.209 million. In the first ten months imports rose 30.6 percent to $88.4 million.</p>
<p>There were no sugar exports in October, compared to $6.693 million in the same month last year. But exports in the first ten months were $22.7 million, unchanged from the same period last year.</p>
<p>-- Saul Hudson, Lima newsroom 511 221-2134</p>
</text>
